  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "A function whose graph is symmetrical about the origin must be odd.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is an even function.<br />Since,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> is an odd function,<br /><math><mo>∴</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is an even function.<br />If <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>∀</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, then<br />Put <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Now, put <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is an odd function",
